[227.054, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I've reworked `pricing.html` in place. I rendered the final page at desktop and mobile widths in headless\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Chrome and looked at it, and the layout and plan selector worked. I made the dark-mode check-icon fix last\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and haven't re-rendered it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What changed from the first version**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Plans:** I restructured them by number of clients, which makes the right plan easy to spot.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Starter:** $0, up to 3 active clients.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Solo:** $15 a month, or $12 billed yearly, up to 25 clients. This is the highlighted \"Most popular\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Pro:** $35 a month, or $28 billed yearly, with unlimited clients.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Finding your plan:** an \"I work with 1–3 / 4–25 / 26+ clients\" selector highlights the matching card\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with a \"Your fit\" tag.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Doubts answered in each card:** all three plan cards carry three short lines, so none of this is buried\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in the FAQ.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Lock-in:** \"Leave anytime. No contract.\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Fees:** \"0% fees from us\", and card payments cost 2.9% + 30¢ via the processor.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - **Export:** CSV and PDF export on every plan, including free.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Fee example:** a new section shows a $1,000 invoice paid by card and by bank transfer, and what you take\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  home.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Refund line:** a plain \"30-day refund on yearly plans\" appears under the paid plans' buttons when Yearly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is selected.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Removed:** the testimonial, which was an invented quote. The \"9 days sooner\" claim went with it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Mobile:** the Solo card comes first on small screens, and the controls fit at 390px.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **How the prices compare with real tools**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  These figures come from third-party review sites, which often disagree with each other, so check each tool's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  own pricing page before you rely on them. I couldn't reach the official pages.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Tool | Free tier | Paid plans (US, monthly) | Client limits |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Wave | $0, unlimited invoices | Pro $19 | – |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | FreshBooks | none | $23 / $43 / $70 | 5 / 50 / unlimited |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Invoice Ninja | yes, 5 clients (one source says 20) | Pro about $10–14, Enterprise $18 | – |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Bonsai | none | $21–25 / $39 / $79 | – |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Your $15 Solo plan is below FreshBooks Lite ($23, 5 clients) and Wave Pro ($19). Your $35 Pro plan is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  between FreshBooks Plus ($43) and Bonsai Professional ($39). Starter's 3-client limit is tighter than\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Invoice Ninja's free tier, which gives more reason to upgrade.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Still placeholders or not covered**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Made-up details:** the product name, the 30-day refund, \"two extra team seats\", API access and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"active clients\" definition are all invented, so confirm each matches your real product.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Processor fees:** the 2.9% + 30¢ card fee and the 0.8% (max $5) bank-transfer fee match typical Stripe\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rates. Check them against your own processor.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Not tested:** I didn't test the live pricing against the first version in a browser beyond the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  screenshots, and I haven't re-rendered after the last dark-mode icon fix.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Working files are in `.ambition/`. The original is in `.ambition/first/`, and snapshots are in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/steps/2/` and `.ambition/steps/3/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
