[242.072, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 3/8 · Depth\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The four statements**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **What a top conversion designer would do that wasn't asked for:** verify every number on the page, run\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  an accessibility and contrast audit, check for overflow at real device widths, and add the invisible launch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  hygiene a shipping page needs (favicon, theme color, structured pricing data).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Rawest material:** the competitors' own pricing pages, not review sites, and the page's own DOM as\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rendered at exact viewports.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Instruments:** WebFetch on the official pricing pages. `puppeteer-core` driving the installed Chrome at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  exact viewports and color schemes. axe-core for the accessibility audit. A script that checks the page's own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  arithmetic (fees, yearly totals, table vs. cards).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **What other than me proves it:** axe-core's report, measured overflow numbers per width, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  competitor pages themselves.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Rewritten task:** verify the benchmarks against official sources, audit the page with real tools, fix what\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  they find, and add the launch hygiene. Same page, deeper.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
