[324.658, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 4/8 · Challenge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions, riskiest first**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Assumption | Who set it | Depends on |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 1 | Card 2.9% + 30¢ and bank transfer 0.8% (max $5) are real processor rates | me | Which processor you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  use |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 2 | Solo $15 and Pro $35 are believable against the market | me | Bonsai's price, still unverified |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 3 | A visitor sees the plans and a CTA without scrolling | me, implicitly | Viewport height |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 4 | Every promise on the page agrees with every other mention of it | me | Copy edits across cards, table\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and FAQ |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 5 | The CTAs lead somewhere that knows which plan was picked | me | Your signup flow |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll test #1 and #2 against the real pages, and #3 and #4 by running the page.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
