[400.467, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 4 report: Challenge**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:** I listed the assumptions and tested each against the real thing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Assumption | How I tested it | Result |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Processor rates are 2.9% + 30¢ and 0.8% (max $5) | Fetched Stripe's pricing page | **Unverified.** Both\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fetches returned the UK page, so the US rates still rest on my memory. Confirm them against your processor.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Prices are believable against the market | Fetched Bonsai's official page | **Held.** Bonsai is $15 / $25\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  / $39 / $59 per user, with invoicing starting at $25. Solo at $15 and Pro at $35 sit under that. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Visitors see plans and a button without scrolling | Measured button positions in headless Chrome at five\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  viewport sizes | **Failed**, see below. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Every promise reads the same everywhere | Pulled every mention of cancel, export, fees and clients from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the rendered page | **Partly failed**, see below. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | CTAs go somewhere that knows the chosen plan | Clicked the billing toggle and read the links | **Fixed**,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  see below. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found (the blind spot):** the Solo button sat below the first screen at 1280×720, at 1366×640 (a very\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  common laptop size) and at 375×667. Visitors had to scroll to find the buy button.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Hero compacted:** the headline and subheading each fit on one line on desktop, and the spacing is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tighter. The Solo button now sits at 536px, so it's above the fold at 1440×800, 1280×720, 1366×640 and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  390×844. At 375×667 the price shows, but the button is still just below the fold. I looked at the result at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1366×640 and 390×844 and it reads cleanly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Export promise unified:** \"even after you cancel\" now appears on all three plan cards, since it was only\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  on Solo before. Starter's \"no cancellation fee\" is now \"nothing to cancel\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Signup links carry the plan:** the buttons now go to `/signup?plan=starter|solo|pro`, with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `&billing=yearly` added on the paid plans when Yearly is selected. I tested this by clicking the toggle.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `/signup` is a placeholder route, so point it at your real signup URL.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Regression checks:** axe still reports 0 violations in light and dark mode, and there's no overflow from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  320 to 1280px.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The step-4 snapshot is in `.ambition/steps/4/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[400.611, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 5 of pushing the work further: Range. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 5/8 · Range`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[431.971, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 5/8 · Range\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the page is really trying to do, as verbs**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Genre verbs:** get a busy freelancer to find their plan, and make them want it enough to start.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Added verbs:** help them compare options and decide, and get them to believe the terms are what they\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  appear to be, even though they've been burned before.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Fields that do this differently**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Field | What they actually do | Direction I took |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Pricing-page designer (the genre's own best practitioner) | One recommended plan, short cards, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  decision on the first screen | Mostly done in earlier steps. I kept the recommendation but changed how the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  badge is worded. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Consumer-finance disclosure (Schumer box, subscription-renewal rules) | Put every cost and every \"what\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  happens when\" case in plain view, including trial end and auto-renewal | Add the trial-end and renewal\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  disclosure, plus a tax line. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Behavioral economist | Show the concrete saving in dollars, and avoid dark patterns | The yearly note now\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  says what you save. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Support-desk triage (the field I wouldn't normally consider) | Read what people ask before buying | Add\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the question freelancers ask most: \"do my clients need an account to pay?\" |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Red team (consumer-protection and accessibility auditor) | Break it, misuse it, find who gets hurt | See\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  below. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Edge I took:** the page a skeptical freelancer can verify. Competitors' pricing pages hide complexity.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  FreshBooks leads with promo prices, and Wave's card fee changes after the first 10 transactions. This page\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  states the whole cost, including trial end and renewal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the red team found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **\"Most popular\" is an unsubstantiated claim** for a new product, which is a deceptive-claim risk. I'm\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  changing it to a recommendation instead of a statistic.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **\"Free forever\" is a promise the business may not keep.** I'm changing it to \"Free, no time limit.\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **No auto-renewal or trial-end disclosure.** That's the classic subscription harm: a surprise charge.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **No tax disclosure.** Prices exclude sales tax and VAT.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  5. **Screen readers get no feedback** when the plan highlight or the yearly prices change.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  6. **Without JavaScript, the controls do nothing.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Now I'll apply these.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[432.97, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd \"<workspace>\" && grep -n 'Most popular\\|Free forever\\|refund\\|billed yearly\\|class=\"note\"\\|<s…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
