[465.674, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 5 report: Range**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:** I read the page as five fields would: a pricing-page designer, consumer-finance disclosure, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  behavioral economist, support-desk triage and a red team. I borrowed one concrete move from each. I did this\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  myself without subagents.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found (red team)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Unsupported claims:** \"Most popular\" can't be backed up for a new product, and \"Free forever\" is a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  promise the business may not keep.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Missing disclosures:** nothing said what happens when the trial ends or that yearly plans renew\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  automatically. That's the usual way subscriptions end up charging people by surprise. There was also no tax\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  line.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Accessibility:** screen readers weren't told when the plan highlight or the billing period changed, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  without JavaScript the controls did nothing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Badge:** it now reads \"Best for most freelancers\", a recommendation instead of a statistic.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Free tier note:** \"Free, no time limit\" replaces \"Free forever\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Trial and renewal terms:** the paid plan cards say the trial ends on Starter with no surprise charge. In\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  yearly view they say \"30-day refund. Renews yearly; we email you first.\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Yearly savings:** the yearly note now shows dollars saved ($36 on Solo, $84 on Pro).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Tax:** the note under the plans says prices are before any sales tax or VAT.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **FAQ:** it now covers trial end, yearly auto-renewal and whether clients need an account to pay. The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"credit card to start?\" question was folded into the trial one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Accessibility fixes:** screen readers get announcements for the plan highlight and the monthly/yearly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  switch, and the controls hide themselves when JavaScript is off.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Checks re-run:** axe still reports 0 violations in light and dark mode, there's no overflow, the signup\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  links still follow the toggle, and the Solo button is still above the fold at the desktop sizes. At 375×667\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it's still just below.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Needs your confirmation:** several of these new statements are product policies I made up as placeholders:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - the 7-day renewal email\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - the 30-day refund\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - clients paying without an account\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - \"two clicks\" to cancel\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - \"two extra team seats\" and API access on Pro\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Please confirm or correct each before launch. On this page, the processor fee rates (2.9% + 30¢, 0.8% capped\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  at $5) are still unverified.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The step-5 snapshot is in `.ambition/steps/5/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
