[564.165, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 6 report: Judge**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Acceptance test:** I wrote `.ambition/tools/accept.mjs`, a script that drives real Chrome and holds the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page to 39 checks. They cover the original ask, every promise in the restatement, and the quality bar. They\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  include:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - self-contained, no JS errors, and three plans with the middle one recommended\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - lock-in, fees and export answered inside every plan card\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - no testimonials, and the arithmetic (yearly totals, savings, fee examples) correct\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the table agreeing with the cards\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the toggle, selector and signup links working\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the Solo button above the fold at four screen sizes\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - no overflow at 320 to 1280px, and 0 axe-core violations in light and dark mode\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the controls hidden when JavaScript is off\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cold read:** I read the whole rendered page text, FAQ opened, start to finish.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rendering:** I looked at desktop and mobile contact sheets, light and dark.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Result:** the final passes 39 of 39 and the first version passes 15 of 39. Some of those first-version\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  failures are fair: no objection answers in the cards, no fee example, the Solo button below the fold, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  two accessibility violations. Others only reflect the new numbers and features, so don't treat 15 versus 39\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  as a pure quality measure.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **No-JS failure:** my first run failed one check. The no-JavaScript rule was losing to the main\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  stylesheet, and I fixed it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cold read, four issues:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - \"Unlimited clients\" appeared twice on the Pro card.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Starter said \"Branded PDF invoices\", which is ambiguous next to Solo's \"no Inkwell branding\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The fees FAQ answered \"Never\" and then listed fees.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - \"Yearly plans renew at the same price\" is a promise I invented.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Visual flaw:** in dark mode the comparison table's \"not included\" dashes were almost invisible.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The duplicate Pro bullet is removed, and Starter now says \"PDF invoices with a small Inkwell footer, sent\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  by email\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The fees answer now opens \"None of our own.\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The table dashes are now clearly visible in both modes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - All 39 checks pass after these fixes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Still open**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Renewal price:** confirm whether the \"same price\" renewal promise is true for your business, or I'll\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  soften it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Processor fees:** the 2.9% + 30¢ and 0.8% (max $5) rates are still unverified.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Small phone:** at 375×667 the Solo button is still just below the fold. The test only covers 390×844.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The step-6 snapshot is in `.ambition/steps/6/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
