[705.72, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The pricing page, `pricing.html`, is finished and passes 39 of 39 checks plus the stretch target. It is a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  single self-contained file for a made-up app called Inkwell. I also built the checks that now guard it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## Report\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A pricing page for a freelancer invoicing app, as a single page → a launch-ready page for signups and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  upgrades.** It is still one file with no dependencies.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A free tier, a mid solo plan and a higher plan → plans split by client count.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Starter is $0 for 5 clients.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Solo is $15 a month, or $12 billed yearly, for 25 clients, and is the recommended plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Pro is $35 a month, or $28 billed yearly, with unlimited clients.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Visitors find their plan in seconds → an \"I work with 1–5 / 6–25 / 26+ clients\" selector** that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  highlights the matching plan, plus a clear \"who it's for\" line on each card.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Doubts about lock-in, fees and export answered by the plans → each plan card carries its own answers.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  There's also a worked fee example showing what you take home and a comparison table.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Your change: no invented testimonials → removed.** A plain refund line stays, and the FAQ covers trial\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  end, renewal and whether clients need an account to pay.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Better on:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The first screen now shows the decision, with the Solo button above the fold at 1366×640, 1280×720 and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  390×844.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The objection answers sit inside each plan card.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The prices, fees and table all agree with each other.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - There are 0 accessibility violations in light and dark mode.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Dark mode is clearer, and nothing overflows from 320 to 1280px.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Gave up:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The first version's testimonial, on purpose.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The cards no longer say \"even after you cancel\" or \"drop back to Starter\". Those details now live only\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in the FAQ.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The subheading is hidden below 860px width.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Check on both:** the same script gives the final 39/39 and the first version 15/39. Part of that gap\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  reflects numbers and features this run introduced, so it isn't a pure quality measure.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **What ran:** real Chrome driven by `puppeteer-core`, plus axe-core for accessibility.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **What it returned:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The yearly totals, savings and fee examples are all arithmetically correct.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The table agrees with the cards.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - There's no overflow at any width, and axe reports 0 violations.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The toggle, selector and signup links work.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The controls hide when JavaScript is off.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Official pricing pages:** Wave, FreshBooks, Invoice Ninja and Bonsai each confirmed the market range.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Target:** at 1366×640 the first screen shows all three plans, prices, buttons and the three objection\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  answers, and at 375×667 the Solo button is above the fold.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **How far it got:** all four sizes pass, 1366×640, 375×667, 390×844 and 1280×720.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **What it cost:** the card wording is shorter, as noted above.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `checks/accept.mjs` runs the 39 acceptance checks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `checks/stretch.mjs` runs the first-screen check.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `checks/package.json` lists the two dependencies.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `CLAUDE.md` explains how to run the checks and what they prove.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `.claude/commands/check-pricing.md` is the `/check-pricing` command.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - To rerun, use `cd checks && npm install && npm run check`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The step snapshots are in `.ambition/steps/2/` through `.ambition/steps/8/`, and the original is in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/first/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions made:** you said to use my judgement only to finish without stopping, so I answered no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  questions on your behalf. The invented product facts are all placeholders: the product name, the 30-day\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  refund, the 7-day renewal email, the two-click cancel, clients paying without an account, two extra team\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  seats on Pro, and API access on Pro.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions left**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Decision | Options | For / against | My pick | Owner, date |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 1 | Card and bank fee rates (2.9% + 30¢, 0.8% max $5) | Confirm against your processor, or soften the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  wording | Confirming makes the page's most important claim true. Softening loses the clarity that is the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page's edge. | Confirm. | You, by 2026-11-18 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 2 | The invented policies listed above | Confirm each, or cut the ones you won't honor | Each confirmed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  claim builds trust. Each false one is a deceptive-claim risk on a real launch. | Confirm or cut each one\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  before launch. | You, by 2026-11-18 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 3 | Prices: Solo $15, Pro $35, Starter 5 clients | Keep, or raise Solo toward $19–23 | Competitors sit at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  $19–23 for similar plans, so $15 undercuts them. $15 may leave money on the table. | Keep at launch, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  revisit after 4 weeks of data. | You, review 2026-12-15 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 4 | Signup links (`/signup?plan=…`) | Point at your real signup, or keep the placeholder | A real URL\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  makes the plan and billing choice carry through. | Point them at the real signup. | You, before launch |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The next check is `/check-pricing` after any edit. A run of `npm run check` is the standing proof.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Metrics since 2026-11-13T01:15:54Z (cost: /cost, or total_cost_usd in headless JSON)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  total   in 168 · out 75.8k (think 23.6k) · cache read 7.47M · write 146.4k · hit 98% · 77 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  model   sonnet-5-5: in 168 · out 75.8k (think 23.6k) · cache read 7.47M · write 146.4k · hit 98% · 77 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n"]
